{# The password of the signed-in person (architecture §5.2), in the language of the browser: when it was
   last written, whether a list of compromised passwords has since found it, the form that replaces it, and
   what that form was refused. Nothing visible changes when a password does, so the date is what a person
   reads after they changed it.

   The page is only reached with a proof given a short while ago (RecentLogin); the password in use is
   typed again on top of that, because a session is not a proof that whoever holds it knows the password,
   and the one posed is typed twice, because a password nobody can read back is a password nobody can check
   they typed right. Changing it signs every other browser out, which the page says before it is asked for.

   The meter beside the new password is the script of the bundle (password-strength.js) and asks nobody
   anything: the words are here, the estimate is the script's, and both rules are the server's whatever it
   showed. "refusal" is a code of AccountPasswordChangeController or of the refusals of the core, and
   "demanded" says that a login was sent here rather than where it was going (issue #579).
   Overridable by an application under templates/bundles/BeffroiBundle/. #}
{% extends '@Beffroi/layout.html.twig' %}
{% trans_default_domain 'beffroi' %}

{% block title %}{{ 'password.title'|trans }}{% endblock %}

{% block head %}
    <script src="{{ path('beffroi_interaction_password_strength_script') }}" defer></script>
{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
    {{ include('@Beffroi/account/back.html.twig') }}
    {% if refusal is not null %}
        <p data-error="{{ refusal }}">{{ ('password.error.' ~ refusal)|trans({minimum: minimum}) }}</p>
    {% endif %}
    {% if federated %}
        {# A person of a federated domain signs in through their organisation (decision 0029): a password
           they held before is replaced by nobody, and none is posed. #}
        <p data-federated>{{ 'account.federated_domain'|trans }}</p>
    {% elseif password is null %}
        {# Somebody who signs in by another means has nothing to replace here, and posing a first one is
           an enrolment, which proves something first. #}
        <p data-password="none">{{ 'password.none'|trans }}</p>
    {% else %}
        <p data-password="{{ password.id }}"><time datetime="{{ password.hashChangedAt|date('c') }}">{{ 'password.changed_at'|trans({date: password.hashChangedAt|beffroi_moment(user)}) }}</time></p>
        {% if password.isBreached() %}
            {# Found after it was posed, by the lane and not by a login (issue #552): the person is told
               here, where they can do something about it. #}
            <p data-password-breached="{{ password.breachFoundAt|date('c') }}">{{ 'password.breached'|trans({date: password.breachFoundAt|beffroi_moment(user)}) }}</p>
            {% if demanded %}
                {# A login that served no authorization request was sent here instead of where it was
                   going (issue #579), and this says so. Nothing holds the browser on this page: the way
                   back to the account is the one every page of it carries. #}
                <p data-password-demanded>{{ 'password.demanded'|trans }}</p>
            {% endif %}
        {% endif %}
        <form method="post" action="{{ path('beffroi_interaction_account_password_change') }}" data-password="change">
            <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token('beffroi_password_change') }}">
            <p>{{ 'password.what_happens'|trans }}</p>
            <label for="password-current">{{ 'password.current'|trans }}</label>
            <input type="password" id="password-current" name="current_password" autocomplete="current-password" required>
            <label for="password-new">{{ 'password.new'|trans }}</label>
            <input type="password" id="password-new" name="new_password" minlength="{{ minimum }}" autocomplete="new-password" required
                   data-password-strength="password-strength"
                   data-strength-floor="{{ floor }}"
                   data-strength-labels="{{ rungs|map(key => key|trans)|json_encode }}">
            <p id="password-strength" data-strength-meter hidden></p>
            <label for="password-again">{{ 'password.again'|trans }}</label>
            <input type="password" id="password-again" name="new_password_again" minlength="{{ minimum }}" autocomplete="new-password" required>
            <button type="submit">{{ 'password.change'|trans }}</button>
        </form>
    {% endif %}
{% endblock %}
